# A project saved before the 303's drive was rescaled (sound revision 5, as 1.1.0 saves, or earlier)
# loads with each 303's DRIVE moved to the pot that drives as it did and its VOLUME to the one that
# keeps its level; a DRIVE lane's steps are mapped too, with a VOLUME lane made for them. Drive 0 is
# left alone. (Values: bass303_pre_rescale; drive303lanes has a VOLUME lane.)
wait 300
# 303 A: RAT, Volume 96, Drive 10, and a p-lock of Drive 30 on step 1
param 2 0 9 2
param 2 0 7 96
param 2 0 8 10
turn ALGO 2
expect part 2
tap SEQ
tapkey w0
expect gate0.0 1
tap EDIT
turn SELECT 1
key w0 down
spin K3 20
key w0 up
expect lanes 1
expect laneval2.0.8.0 30
# 303 B: Soft, Volume 96, Drive 64
param 2 1 9 1
param 2 1 7 96
param 2 1 8 64
sndrev 5
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 300
expect lanes 2
expect sound2.0.8 86
expect sound2.0.7 106
expect laneval2.0.8.0 102
expect laneval2.0.7.0 109
expect sound2.1.8 42
expect sound2.1.7 88
# saved again: now revision 7, nothing moves a second time
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 300
expect lanes 2
expect sound2.0.8 86
expect sound2.0.7 106
expect laneval2.0.8.0 102
expect laneval2.0.7.0 109
# drive 0: the pots as they were
param 2 1 8 0
param 2 1 7 96
sndrev 5
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 300
expect sound2.1.8 0
expect sound2.1.7 96
# from revision 4 (before the break's FILTER, its pot then an unused 0): both revisions apply, the
# filter off and the 303's drive as before (303 B: Soft, Volume 96, Drive 64, as above)
param 2 1 8 64
param 2 1 7 96
param 3 0 2 0
sndrev 4
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 300
expect sound3.0.2 64
expect sound2.1.8 42
expect sound2.1.7 88
